              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lōrum, lōrī — \"a leather strap, a thong; (plural) reins\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Servus sarcinās lōrīs ad mūlum ligat. The slave ties the bags to the mule with straps."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, neuter: lōrum, lōrī n. A strap of leather for tying, for reins, or for whipping."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lōrum is inherited. Lewis & Short compare Greek eulēra 'reins' and suggest an older form vlōrum; EtymDB gives no parent, so the link is hedged."
            }
          ]
        },
